      "extract": "INTRODUCTION Matter composed of neutrons and protons exhibits remarkable properties. Cold neutron matter is close to a scaling regime for densities n ≲1/10 n0, where n0 = 0.16 fm−3 denotes nuclear saturation density. In this regime, thermodynamic properties of neutron mat- ter scale only with the density, and for the energy per particle E/N one has approximately [1, 2] E N ≈0.5 \u0012 E N \u0013 free = 0.5 3(3π2)2/3 10m n2/3",
      "extractCut": true
    },
